      "summary": "A Comment on Gurney et al (2026 Environ. Res. Lett.21 094018); G26) attributes our finding of a 70.4% mean relative difference (MRD) between Climate TRACE (CT) and Vulcan urban on-road CO2 emissions to a since-corrected error in one CT release, reporting an 8.6% MRD using corrected data. We ’s claimed correction date, but set this timing question aside to focus on more substantive concerns. The cited correction is a single multiplicative rescaling that, by construction, can—biases the Comment does ’s own claims of unprecedented spatial granularity. We further show that the national- and county-scale ‘agreement’ the Comment cites is uninformative about the sub-national accuracy G26 actually assessed, since CT’s national totals are explicitly calibrated to EDGAR by construction, while county-level differences remain large and widely dispersed. Vulcan’s own independent validation record—against atmospheric radiocarbon inversion, traffic count, and EPA state-level estimates—su’s recommendation that CT’s on-road emissions estimates be used with caution pending independent, peer-reviewed validation remains fully justified.",
